{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-53701",
    "CVE-2026-53702"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that GStreamer Bad Plugins incorrectly handled parsing\nH.266/VVC picture partition data. An attacker could use this issue to cause\nGStreamer Bad Plugins to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or\npossibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-53701)\n\nIt was discovered that GStreamer Bad Plugins incorrectly handled parsing\nH.265 buffering period metadata. An attacker could use this issue to cause\nGStreamer Bad Plugins to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or\npossibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-53702)",
  "id": "USN-8446-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in GStreamer Bad Plugins.",
